Package: shieldR
Title: Simulation of Evacuation Policies under Uncertainty
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("R.", "Heller",
    email = "58561665+r-heller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A research implementation of a five-leg evacuation-chain
    simulation with patient deterioration, imperfect reassessment, finite
    vehicle resources, route-risk beliefs, and static or adaptive disruption-risk
    responses. Supports reproducible policy comparisons and paired
    disruptions-disabled interventions. Includes neutral teaching scenarios and
    nonparametric analysis helpers. The model is a synthetic research
    framework; its decision heuristics have no established clinical or
    operational validity.
